# Mobile `pnpm dev` loads `apps/api/.env` first — put EXPO_PUBLIC_* there so Metro sees them.
# You can also put the same keys in this file (`apps/mobile/.env`); Expo reads it for Metro.
# Copy apps/api/.env.example → apps/api/.env and set keys/URLs there.
#
# LOCAL DEV: always use the local Nest API (port 3010).
# Android emulator → http://10.0.2.2:3010
# iOS Simulator → http://127.0.0.1:3010
# Physical phone over USB (adb reverse) → http://127.0.0.1:3010
# Physical phone over Wi‑Fi → http://YOUR_LAN_IP:3010
# PRODUCTION BUILDS ONLY: set EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL / SOCKET to the Render backend.
# Do not leave Render as the active URL while developing in the simulator.
#
# Restart Expo after any change (`expo start --clear` if the URL looks wrong).
#
# Example for USB physical device:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3010
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3010
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
